# AD inventory — {{ lab_name }}

> **Contains real NT password hashes from a live deployment** (pass-the-hash
> usable directly, and crackable offline — `hashcat -m 1000`). This file
> lives in `generated/{{ lab_name }}/` (gitignored) — never commit it, never
> share it outside this lab's authorized operators. This is a POST-DEPLOY
> snapshot, not reproducible from the spec: BadBlood's own per-user
> passwords are randomly generated with PowerShell's `Get-Random` on the DC
> during `site.yml` and never written anywhere, not even by BadBlood itself
> — this file exists because NT hashes (unlike plaintext) genuinely are
> stored in AD and recoverable via DCSync. Regenerate anytime the domain
> changes with `python3 scripts/forge.py ad-inventory <spec>`; it always
> reflects whatever the domain looks like *right now*, not what was
> originally intended (see `lab-report.md` for that).

